From: Dan <dan@awto.au>
Subject: [PATCH] realtek: l3: use the fib_offload library

Applied after 300-17 and 300-21. l3.c keeps the RTL93xx table logic
(row placement, trap and catch-all rows, host slots, DMAC/egress
allocation, router MACs, debugfs); the kernel-facing plumbing moves to
net/core/fib_offload.c (docs/UPSTREAM-L3.md, #85):

- FIB/rule notifiers, work items, table filter, dump flush and replay
  after a lost event: library; l3.c gets ->fib_event / ->flush.
- Policy rules: evaluated by the library (same algorithm, same log
  line); ->fwd_suspend does what otto_l3_rules_check() did.
- netevent: library; ->neigh_update does nexthop + on-link updates.
- The RTNL poll every DELAY_PROBE_TIME is gone:
  - stale-neighbour refresh: library ->nh_hit() on NUD_STALE events and
    while stale (same hit read/clear as the poll);
  - next hops without an L2 entry: fib_offload_nh_retry() from
    otto_l3_route_update_hw(), retried every DELAY_PROBE_TIME;
  - l3_onlink / l3_default_v4 / l3_default_v6: module_param_cb, applied
    on write (and once at probe for the command line);
  - default rows also re-checked after each neighbour event.
- IPv4 routes now report offload / trap / offload_failed through
  fib_alias_hw_flags_set (was RTNH_F_OFFLOAD on the nexthop); RTL839x
  keeps RTNH_F_OFFLOAD.
- Module parameters, log lines and table contents unchanged.
---
